{title: Boldly I Approach (FJ_17_en)}
{song_number: 17}
{language: en}
{key: Em}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[Em]By grace alone somehow I stand [Dsus4]where even angels fear to [C]tread;
[Em]invited by redeeming love [Dsus4]before the throne of God a[C]bove.
[G/B]He pulls me close with [C]nail-scarred [D]hands [Em]into His ever[C]lasting arms. [Dsus4][G]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[Em]Boldly I approach Your [C]throne, [D]blameless now I'm running [Em]home.
[G/B]By Your blood I [C]come, welcomed [D]as Your [Em]own,
in[C]to the arms of [D]majes[G]ty.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[Em]When condemnation grips my heart [Dsus4]and Satan tempts me to de[C]spair,
[Em]I hear the voice that scatters fear; [Dsus4]the Great I Am, the Lord is [C]here.
[G/B]O, praise the One who [C]fights for [D]me [Em]and shields my soul e[C]ternally. [Dsus4][G]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[Em]Boldly I approach Your [C]throne, [D]blameless now I'm running [Em]home.
[G/B]By Your blood I [C]come, welcomed [D]as Your [Em]own,
in[C]to the arms of [D]majes[G]ty.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[Em]Behold the bright and risen Son, [Dsus4]more beauty than this world has [C]known.
[Em]I'm face to face with Love Himself; [Dsus4]His perfect spotless righteous[C]ness.
[G/B]A thousand years, a [C]thousand [D]tongues [Em]are not enough to [C]sing His praise. [Dsus4][G]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[Em]Boldly I approach Your [C]throne, [D]blameless now I'm running [Em]home.
[G/B]By Your blood I [C]come, welcomed [D]as Your [Em]own,
in[C]to the arms of [D]majes[G]ty.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge}
[C]This is the art of cele[G]bration, [D]knowing we're free from condem[C]nation.
[G]O, praise the One, [D]praise the One [Em7]who made an end to [C]all my [D]sin. [G]
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus}
[Em]Boldly I approach Your [C]throne, [D]blameless now I'm running [Em]home.
[G/B]By Your blood I [C]come, welcomed [D]as Your [Em]own,
in[C]to the arms of [D]majes[G]ty.
